// AUTHORED RESTATEMENT BATCH 002 — B1, B2 and C1.
//
// Same design as batch 001: every item's three distractors use three
// different traps — logic_flip, agent_swap, timing_shift — so a wrong answer
// says WHICH kind of misreading the user makes, not merely that one happened.
// The correct answer is re-worded end to end rather than shuffled, so it
// cannot be found by matching vocabulary against the source.
//
// STATUS: stage 3 only. Not blind-checked, not shippable.
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "The library extended its opening hours last winter, but the number of borrowed books stayed almost exactly the same.", "correct_answer": "Keeping the doors unlocked for longer over the cold months produced no real change in how much people read.", "distractors": [{"text": "Because borrowing stayed at the same level, the library decided to extend its opening hours last winter.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Readers themselves extended the library's opening hours, though the number of books borrowed hardly changed.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The library will extend its opening hours next winter in the hope that more books are borrowed.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The longer hours came first and changed nothing. The first wrong option makes the unchanged borrowing the reason for the longer hours. The second gives readers a power only the library has. The third moves a finished experiment into the future.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Although the new bus route reaches the hospital in half the time, very few passengers have chosen to use it.", "correct_answer": "Hardly anyone travels on the service despite it cutting the journey to the medical centre by fifty per cent.", "distractors": [{"text": "Because so many passengers now use the new route, the journey to the hospital takes half the time.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Hospital staff selected the new bus route, although very few other passengers travel on it.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The new bus route will halve the journey time once enough passengers agree to use it.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The route is much faster and still almost empty. The first wrong option makes heavy use the reason for the speed. The second invents hospital staff as the ones who chose it. The third makes the time saving depend on future demand.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "The teacher marked the essays before the holiday, and returned them to the students on the first day back.", "correct_answer": "Grading was finished ahead of the break, with each piece of work handed over as soon as classes resumed.", "distractors": [{"text": "The teacher gave the essays back before the holiday and marked them once the students returned.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Students marked one another's essays over the holiday and gave them to the teacher afterwards.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The teacher will mark the essays during the holiday and hand them back when term begins.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Marking happened before the holiday and handing back after it. The first wrong option reverses those two events. The second makes the students the markers. The third leaves the marking still to be done.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Prices in the market fall every autumn, because farmers harvest more fruit than the town can possibly eat.", "correct_answer": "Each year the crop is bigger than local appetite, so what shoppers pay drops when the season arrives.", "distractors": [{"text": "Farmers grow extra fruit in autumn because prices in the market have already come down.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Traders in the town cut their prices every autumn so that farmers will gather more fruit.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Prices are expected to fall next autumn if farmers gather more fruit than usual.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "A surplus of fruit is what pushes prices down. The first wrong option makes the low prices the reason for growing more. The second makes traders act in order to influence farmers. The third turns a yearly pattern into a single forecast.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "The village had no doctor for eleven years, until a clinic opened in the old school building last spring.", "correct_answer": "Medical care returned to the settlement only when premises were converted for that purpose, after more than a decade.", "distractors": [{"text": "A clinic opened in the old school eleven years before the village lost its last doctor.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The village doctor opened a clinic in the old school building after eleven years of waiting.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The village still has no doctor, but a clinic is due to open in the old school.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Eleven years without a doctor ended when the clinic opened. The first wrong option puts the clinic before the gap instead of after it. The second invents a village doctor who was in fact absent. The third leaves the clinic unopened.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Most of the students who failed the first test passed easily when they took it again in June.", "correct_answer": "Nearly everyone unsuccessful at the initial attempt found the repeat straightforward a few months later.", "distractors": [{"text": "Most students who succeeded at the first test were unable to pass when they sat it a second time.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The examiners passed most of the failing students without asking them to sit the paper again.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Students who failed the first test will be allowed to take it again in June.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Those who failed first time went on to succeed second time. The first wrong option swaps which attempt was the successful one. The second removes the resit and makes the examiners award the pass. The third turns a completed resit into a future permission.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "The factory produces twice as much as it did five years ago, but employs fewer than half the workers.", "correct_answer": "Output has doubled over that period while the number of people on the payroll has more than halved.", "distractors": [{"text": "The factory now employs twice as many staff but makes less than half of what it once did.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Workers at the factory have halved their own numbers in order to double what the machines make.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The factory expects to double its output and halve its workforce within the next five years.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Production doubled and staffing more than halved. The first wrong option swaps which figure rose and which fell. The second makes the workers themselves responsible for cutting the workforce. The third turns a measured change into a plan.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "She refused the promotion twice before accepting a similar role at a smaller company the following year.", "correct_answer": "After turning down the senior post on two occasions, she took an equivalent job elsewhere twelve months later.", "distractors": [{"text": "She accepted the promotion immediately and turned down a comparable position at a smaller company afterwards.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The smaller company rejected her twice before offering the senior position she had wanted.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "She has refused the promotion twice and may accept a comparable position elsewhere next year.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Two refusals came first, then an equivalent job somewhere else. The first wrong option reverses which offer she accepted. The second makes the company the one doing the rejecting. The third leaves the second job undecided.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The council approved the development only after the builder agreed to fund a new road to the site.", "correct_answer": "Permission was granted purely on condition that the construction firm paid for improved access itself.", "distractors": [{"text": "The builder agreed to fund the new road only after the council had already approved the development.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The council undertook to build the new road itself once the developer's application had been approved.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The council will approve the development if the builder promises to fund a new road.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The builder's promise came first and the approval followed. The first wrong option reverses that order. The second makes the council pay for the road. The third turns a decision already taken into a condition still to be met.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Because the samples were stored at the wrong temperature, the laboratory had to repeat the entire experiment.", "correct_answer": "Incorrect refrigeration of the material forced staff to run the whole study a second time.", "distractors": [{"text": "The samples were kept at the wrong temperature because the experiment had to be carried out twice.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The scientists blamed the delivery company for repeating the experiment with badly stored samples.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "If the samples are kept at the wrong temperature, the laboratory will have to repeat the experiment.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Bad storage is why the work had to be done again. The first wrong option makes the repetition the reason for the bad storage. The second hands the repeat to an outside company. The third turns a completed setback into a warning.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The treaty allows each country to inspect the other's facilities twice a year, without giving advance notice.", "correct_answer": "Under the agreement either state may examine its counterpart's installations on two occasions annually with no warning beforehand.", "distractors": [{"text": "Each country must give advance notice before entering the other's facilities, which it may do twice yearly.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "An international body examines the facilities of both countries twice a year without warning them first.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "From next year the treaty will let each country enter the other's facilities twice annually.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Each side may inspect the other twice yearly with no warning. The first wrong option adds the notice the treaty removes. The second replaces the two countries with an outside inspector. The third makes a rule already in force begin later.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Sales rose sharply in the months after the advertisement was withdrawn, which surprised almost everyone at the agency.", "correct_answer": "Removing the commercial was followed by a steep climb in revenue that few people working there had predicted.", "distractors": [{"text": "The advertisement was pulled because sales had already risen sharply, to the surprise of the agency.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Advertisers withdrew from the agency, whose own sales rose sharply in the months afterwards.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Sales are expected to rise sharply once the advertisement is withdrawn later this year.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The advertisement went first and the rise came afterwards. The first wrong option makes the rise the reason for withdrawing it. The second changes what was withdrawn and whose sales rose. The third turns a recorded rise into a forecast.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Inspectors closed the plant after discovering that waste had been discharged into the river for several months.", "correct_answer": "The site was shut down when officials found a long-running release of pollution into local water.", "distractors": [{"text": "Waste was released into the river after inspectors had already closed the plant down.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The plant's owners closed it themselves and reported the discharge to the inspectors.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Inspectors will close the plant if they find that waste has been released into the river.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The discharge came first and the closure followed the discovery. The first wrong option puts the pollution after the closure. The second makes the owners close the plant and report themselves. The third turns a completed shutdown into a threat.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Although the equipment was donated free of charge, installing it cost the hospital more than buying it would have.", "correct_answer": "Setting up the gift proved dearer for the medical centre than a straightforward purchase.", "distractors": [{"text": "The hospital paid for the equipment because accepting a donation would have cost even more.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The hospital donated the equipment and paid another organisation to install it free of charge.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The equipment will be donated free of charge, though installation is expected to be expensive.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The gift was free but fitting it cost more than buying would have. The first wrong option has the hospital buy rather than accept the donation. The second makes the hospital the donor. The third puts an accomplished expense in the future.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The editor rejected the article twice, but published it without changes once a rival journal expressed interest.", "correct_answer": "Two refusals were reversed the moment a competing publication showed enthusiasm, and the piece appeared unaltered.", "distractors": [{"text": "The editor printed the article twice before a rival journal turned it down without explanation.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "A rival journal turned the article down twice, and the editor printed it once interest appeared.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The editor will print the article unchanged if a rival journal shows any interest in it.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Two rejections were followed by unchanged publication once a competitor showed interest. The first wrong option swaps which act happened twice. The second moves the rejections to the rival journal. The third makes the publication conditional and future.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Farmers in the valley abandoned the traditional crop when a cheaper import made it impossible to compete.", "correct_answer": "Growers gave up their old variety because goods arriving from abroad undercut them completely.", "distractors": [{"text": "A cheaper import appeared in the valley because farmers there had already given up the traditional crop.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Importers gave up the traditional crop once farmers in the valley began selling it more cheaply.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Farmers in the valley will give up the traditional crop if a cheaper import reaches the market.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The cheap import is what drove the crop out. The first wrong option makes the abandonment the reason for the import. The second swaps the roles of importers and farmers. The third turns a completed change into a possibility.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The medicine works only when taken with food, which many patients discover after their first ineffective dose.", "correct_answer": "A meal must accompany the drug for it to have any effect, as people often learn the hard way.", "distractors": [{"text": "The medicine works only on an empty stomach, which patients realise after eating with their first dose.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Doctors take the first dose with food in order to find out whether the medicine works.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Patients will be told to take the medicine with food once the first trial results are published.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Food is required for the drug to work at all. The first wrong option reverses the condition to an empty stomach. The second makes doctors rather than patients take the dose. The third replaces present practice with a future instruction.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Rents in the district doubled within three years, forcing many long-established shops to move to cheaper streets.", "correct_answer": "A hundred per cent rise in what businesses paid over that short period pushed old traders elsewhere.", "distractors": [{"text": "Shops moved away to cheaper streets, and rents in the district doubled as a result.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Shopkeepers doubled the rents over three years, which forced the district's landlords to move away.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Rents in the district are likely to double, which would force many old shops to move away.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The rent rise is what drove the shops out. The first wrong option makes the departures the cause of the rise. The second has tenants setting rents and landlords leaving. The third turns a recorded doubling into a prediction.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The bank refused the loan not because the business was unprofitable but because its records were incomplete.", "correct_answer": "Missing paperwork, rather than any lack of earnings, is what led the lender to turn the application down.", "distractors": [{"text": "The bank turned the application down because the business was losing money, although its paperwork was in order.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The business turned down the bank's offer because the paperwork the lender supplied was incomplete.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The bank will turn the application down unless the business completes its paperwork before the deadline.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Incomplete records, not poor profits, explain the refusal. The first wrong option swaps the reason given for the reason denied. The second makes the business the party that refuses. The third turns a decision already made into a warning.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Volunteers cleared the beach every weekend, yet the amount of plastic washed ashore did not noticeably decrease.", "correct_answer": "Weekly unpaid clean-ups made no visible difference to how much rubbish the sea kept depositing on the sand.", "distractors": [{"text": "Plastic stopped arriving on the shore, so volunteers no longer needed to clear the beach at weekends.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The local council cleared the beach each weekend while volunteers measured the plastic arriving there.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Volunteers will clear the beach every weekend until the plastic arriving there begins to fall.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Regular clearing failed to reduce the incoming plastic. The first wrong option ends the problem and with it the clearing. The second gives the work to the council and the measuring to the volunteers. The third turns a completed effort into an ongoing plan.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The species survived the drought in the north but disappeared completely from the drier valleys further south.", "correct_answer": "Populations endured the dry spell at the upper end of the range while vanishing entirely lower down.", "distractors": [{"text": "The species died out in the north but came through the drought in the drier southern valleys.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Farmers in the southern valleys removed the species, which continued to live on in the north.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The species is expected to come through the coming drought in the north but not further south.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "It held on in the north and was lost in the south. The first wrong option swaps the two regions. The second invents farmers as the cause of the southern loss. The third turns a past drought into one still to come.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Students who took notes by hand remembered more of the lecture than those who typed on laptops.", "correct_answer": "Writing with a pen produced better recall of the talk than using a keyboard did.", "distractors": [{"text": "Students working on laptops retained more of the lecture than those writing with a pen.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Lecturers who wrote by hand were remembered better than those who used a laptop in class.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Students will be asked to write their notes by hand so that they retain more of the lecture.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Handwriting beat typing for memory. The first wrong option reverses which group did better. The second makes the lecturers rather than the students the ones writing. The third turns a finding into an instruction not yet given.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "Had the warning been issued a week earlier, the evacuation could have been completed before the storm arrived.", "correct_answer": "Seven more days of notice would have allowed everyone to leave safely ahead of the bad weather.", "distractors": [{"text": "The alert came a week early, which is why everyone had left before the storm arrived.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Residents issued their own alert a week before the storm and left the area in time.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "If the alert is given a week earlier next time, everyone will be able to leave before the storm.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The warning was late and the evacuation was therefore unfinished. The first wrong option treats the imagined early warning as something that actually happened. The second makes the residents issue it. The third turns a regret about the past into a plan for a future storm.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "The measure reduced accidents on the busiest roads, though it had no effect at all on quieter routes.", "correct_answer": "Crashes fell where traffic was heaviest, but nothing changed along less crowded stretches.", "distractors": [{"text": "The measure cut crashes on the emptier stretches while leaving the heaviest traffic entirely unaffected.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Drivers on the busiest roads introduced the measure themselves, and crashes fell as a result.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The measure is expected to cut crashes on the busiest roads once it comes into force.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "It worked where traffic was heavy and nowhere else. The first wrong option swaps which kind of road benefited. The second makes drivers rather than an authority impose it. The third turns a measured result into an expectation.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "What appears to be generosity is often self-interest, since donors gain influence that money could not otherwise buy.", "correct_answer": "Apparent kindness frequently serves the giver, who acquires a standing no payment on its own would secure.", "distractors": [{"text": "People give because they already hold influence, not in order to obtain any for themselves.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Those who receive the gifts gain the standing that the giver's money could never have purchased.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Givers will eventually acquire influence if their apparent kindness continues for long enough.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Giving looks selfless but wins the giver influence. The first wrong option reverses cause and effect by making existing influence the motive. The second transfers the benefit to the recipient. The third turns a general truth into a future outcome.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "The author revised the manuscript for nine years, yet reviewers criticised precisely the passages she had rewritten most.", "correct_answer": "Nearly a decade of reworking produced exactly the sections that critics singled out for attack.", "distractors": [{"text": "Reviewers praised the very sections the author had reworked most during her nine years of revision.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Reviewers spent nine years reworking the manuscript, and the author attacked the sections they changed.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The author intends to spend nine years reworking the sections that reviewers have attacked.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The most reworked passages drew the harshest criticism. The first wrong option turns the criticism into praise. The second makes the reviewers the revisers and the author the critic. The third makes the long revision a future intention.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "Because so few records survive from that century, historians rely heavily on the accounts of a single traveller.", "correct_answer": "The scarcity of remaining documents leaves scholars dependent almost entirely on what one visitor wrote down.", "distractors": [{"text": "Historians ignore the lone traveller's testimony because so much other material from the period is available.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "A single traveller collected the few documents from the period on which scholars now depend.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Scholars will have to depend on one traveller's testimony once the remaining documents are lost.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Because almost nothing else survives, one traveller's account carries the weight. The first wrong option reverses the scarcity and the dependence. The second turns the traveller into a collector of other people's documents. The third places the dependence in a future that has not arrived.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "The policy was defended on economic grounds, although its architects had originally proposed it for entirely political reasons.", "correct_answer": "Money became the public justification for a plan its designers first put forward to serve party purposes.", "distractors": [{"text": "The plan was first put forward to improve the economy and only later justified in political terms.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Opponents of the plan, rather than the people who wrote it, argued that its aims were political.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The plan will be justified in economic terms once its political origins have been forgotten.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Political motives came first, economic arguments came later. The first wrong option swaps the two around. The second moves the political claim from the authors to their opponents. The third makes an existing defence something still to come.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "Only after the third audit did anyone notice that the same signature appeared on every one of the receipts.", "correct_answer": "It took three separate examinations before it became clear that a single hand had signed all the documents.", "distractors": [{"text": "The identical handwriting was spotted immediately, which is why a third examination was eventually ordered.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The people carrying out the examinations had themselves signed all the documents, as nobody realised.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "A third examination will be needed before anyone can check whether the handwriting on the documents matches.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The pattern went unnoticed until the third check. The first wrong option claims it was seen at once. The second makes the auditors the forgers. The third leaves the third check still to happen.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "The invention spread quickly across the continent, but it took almost two centuries to reach the islands offshore.", "correct_answer": "What moved rapidly through the mainland needed nearly two hundred years to arrive on the outlying land masses.", "distractors": [{"text": "The device appeared first on the outlying islands and only moved onto the mainland two hundred years later.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Islanders carried the device to the mainland, where it then moved rapidly for two hundred years.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The device is moving rapidly across the mainland and should reach the outlying islands within two hundred years.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "It travelled fast on land and reached the islands only much later. The first wrong option reverses which place had it first. The second makes islanders the carriers. The third turns a completed spread into one still under way.", "difficulty_est": 5}
